{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs62ygpn5TZGqdvZCPvQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `contacts/dedupe.py`, and the tests pass (1 test). I also ran a quick check of the other cases from the support reports, and it behaved as expected.\n\nThere were three root causes, all in `name_key`:\n1. **Hand-written accent list.** It only handled a few letters, so `í`, `ú`, `ç`, `ê` and many others were never stripped. It now decomposes with Unicode NFKD and drops combining marks, so every accent is covered.\n2. **Mac vs. Windows text.** Macs often store `ü` as `u` plus a combining mark, while Windows uses the single character `ü`. The old code treated those as different names. NFKD decomposition makes both forms identical. It also turns non-breaking spaces into plain spaces before whitespace is collapsed.\n3. **`ß` vs `ss`.** `.lower()` leaves `ß` alone. I switched to `.casefold()`, which turns it into `ss`.\n\nI also changed `email_key` to NFKC normalization plus `casefold()`, so emails get the same Unicode handling. The first-seen record still survives.\n\nOne behaviour you might not expect: a record dropped as a duplicate doesn't register its own email. In my check, a later record that shared only that dropped record's email was kept. The old code did the same thing. Say so if you want dropped records' emails to count too."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9143,"cache_read_input_tokens":33236,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9143},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b5fb529-a9b4-4bef-b573-988d91dd19af","uuid":"f0e412e9-8ed4-43d8-adde-cb8cded98ffc","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:51:13.788Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs62yNjDjA9xFEgQC3uk"}
